1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,941
Jason returned to Vice City owing a
ferry fare. Lucia returned carrying

2
00:00:04,941 --> 00:00:07,000
the fare box's only key.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,250
They'd stolen the key before leaving
town. Tonight, the kiosk operator had

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,000
replaced the collection box.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,278
Jason wanted to force it. Lucia noticed
yesterday's ticket price still

6
00:00:18,278 --> 00:00:21,000
printed above a freshly painted price
board.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,444
The box wasn't new. Someone had dressed
the old one backward to hide the

8
00:00:26,444 --> 00:00:28,000
lock from passing thieves.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,529
Jason lifted the flap. Lucia reached
underneath, found their keyhole, and

10
00:00:32,529 --> 00:00:35,000
opened the box without a sound.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,278
Inside, cash sat beside unpaid ferry
stubs. The operator had been

12
00:00:39,278 --> 00:00:42,000
pocketing fares without issuing the
matching tickets.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,056
They took the notes and bought two real
tickets from the machine. Jason

14
00:00:47,056 --> 00:00:49,000
asked why she bothered paying.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,500
Because, Lucia said, tomorrow somebody
counts passengers. Tonight, we're

16
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,000
the only customers whose money actually
reached the ferry.
